# Template: Front-End Log-Based Development

## File Purpose and Relationship

This file provides a specialized template for log-based front-end development requirements in the PolygonExpress project. It focuses solely on giving structure to the initial requirements.md file for features that will use strategic logging.

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file is a Manual rule type and should be referenced as a project-rule-parameter in the plan-mode message-command:

```
plan-mode: front-end-workflow @parameters/front-end/plan-mode/template-log-based.mdc
```

## Requirements Template

When this template is applied, it will create the following structure in requirements.md:

```markdown
# Log-Based Feature Requirements

## Objective
[What is the purpose of this feature?]

## Functional Requirements
[What functionality should this feature provide?]

## State Management Requirements
[What state needs to be managed and tracked?]

## Logging Strategy Requirements
[What events, state changes, and interactions should be logged?]

Key logging points:
- [Log point 1]: [Description and purpose]
- [Log point 2]: [Description and purpose]
- [Log point 3]: [Description and purpose]

## Verification Points
[What specific state transitions or interactions need verification through logs?]

## Log Format Requirements
[What information should each log entry contain?]

## Debug Mode Requirements
[What additional information should be included in debug mode logs?]

## Performance Considerations
[How should logging impact performance?]

## Success Criteria
[How will we know this feature is implemented correctly through log analysis?]
```

## Template Application

When the template is applied, I will:
1. Create or update requirements.md with this template
2. Leave all sections empty for completion
3. Wait for the requirements to be completed before proceeding with any planning

## Next Steps
1. Complete the requirements template with log-based feature details
2. Once requirements are complete, proceed with planning the implementation approach

## Use Cases
- Complex state management features
- Features requiring detailed debugging
- User interaction tracking
- API interaction verification
- Performance monitoring
- Error tracking and diagnostics 